codex
The missed family is specifically expression statements whose erased value type is `!`: statement lowering ignores the expression result and therefore can continue from a block that Rust already considers divergent. I’m going to make Verus-erased ghost statements produce a unit-typed placeholder for statement/block reachability while still preserving their child checks.
