codex
The remaining missed case is a block whose own type is `!` only because it contains an erased `!` statement. The inner statement is fixed, but the enclosing block expression still carries the old `!` type and can poison reachability. I’m adding recursive detection for ignored block expressions whose divergence comes from an erased statement, and retyping those synthetic block statements to unit as well.
