Root cause / current fix:
Rust MIR construction and post-build pruning treat Verus-erased ghost placeholders with uninhabited result types as real divergence. That removes reachability to later proof statements, so Rust borrow checking misses double use of tracked resources. Current patch preserves return edges for synthetic `erased_ghost_value` calls and handles several ignored statement forms by retyping erased `!` placeholders to unit. This fixes the reported program and many variants, but it is not yet general: nested block-tail erased `!` expressions still leave later code unreachable.

